TI  - Demand prediction method for total knee joint            replacement (TKR) in clinical auxiliary decision,            involves classifying output probability value of TKA            based on set risk threshold and visualized using color            coding, structural heatmaps, or Shapley interpretation            diagrams
AB  - 
                   NOVELTY - The method involves acquiring (S1) MRI images                of the knee joint, and automatically segmenting the                structure into several portions to obtain the                volume of interest (ROI) for each structure. The                image feature is extracted. The SERA radiomics                feature extraction tool is used (S2) to extract                radiomics features from the RIO region. The                clinical symptom score data for the corresponding                patients is obtained (S3), including scores from                the Knee Osteoarthritis Outcome Survey (KOOS)                scale. The Radiomics features and KOOS score                features are fused and input (S4) into the                prediction model to output the probability value of                future TKA. The output probability value of TKA is                classified (S5) based on a set risk threshold and                visualized using color coding, structural heatmaps,                or Shapley interpretation diagrams.
                    USE - Demand prediction method for total knee joint                replacement (TKR) in clinical auxiliary decision                for treating knee osteoarthritis in middle-aged and                elderly population.
                    ADVANTAGE - The method uses LASSO characteristic screening                and shallow neural network modelling, combines with                the Jurdon index setting threshold value. The                prediction performance is better than the existing                model, which obviously improves the consistency and                accuracy of the inpatient to TKR time judgment, and                realizes the intelligent risk intervention before                operation.
                    DETAILED DESCRIPTION - INDEPENDENT CLAIMS are included for: (1) a                demand prediction system for total knee joint                replacement; (2) a computer readable storage                medium.
                    DESCRIPTION Of DRAWING(S) - The drawing shows a flow diagram of the                demand prediction method for total knee joint                replacement. (Drawing includes non-English language                text)S1Step for acquiring MRI images of the knee                jointS2Step for using SERA radiomics feature                extraction toolS3Step for obtaining clinical symptom score                data for the corresponding patientsS4Step for fusing and inputting radiomics                features and KOOS score featuresS5Step for classifying output probability                value of TKA
